      "content": "According to HACCP guidelines, cooked poultry should be cooled to a safe temperature of 74°F (23°C) or below within 2 hours, with the rate of cooling being at least 1°C (1.8°F) per hour. This can be achieved by either hot water bath, cold water bath, or using ice packs to cool the poultry. It's essential to ensure the cooked poultry is not left at or above 40°F (4°C) for an extended period.",
